---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '25 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use · Belal Zaky"
  description="Terms of use for Mission Control, a personal single-user desktop dashboard that reads bank account data through Enable Banking."
>
  <article class="legal container container--prose">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="legal-kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="legal-dek">
        These terms cover <strong>Mission Control</strong>, a personal desktop application I built
        and use myself. It is not a commercial product and it is not offered to anyone else.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What the application is</h2>
      <p>
        Mission Control is a desktop dashboard written and operated by Belal Zaky, an individual
        based in London, United Kingdom. It runs entirely on my own computer. One part of it reads
        my own bank accounts so that I can see my own spending.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>
        Me, and only me. There is no public version, no hosted version, no sign-up, no accounts, and
        no way for another person to use it or to connect their bank to it. Nothing about it is sold,
        licensed, distributed or advertised. If any of that changes, these terms will be rewritten
        first.
      </p>

      <h2>What it does with bank data</h2>
      <p>
        The application uses
        <a href="https://enablebanking.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Enable Banking</a>,
        a licensed account information service provider (AISP), to read account balances and booked
        transactions from banks where I hold accounts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Access is <strong>read-only</strong>. The application has no payment initiation capability. It
        cannot move money, set up transfers, alter standing orders, or change anything at the bank.
      </p>
      <p>
        Access depends on consent I give through my bank's own authorisation screen. That consent is
        time-limited under PSD2 and UK Open Banking rules, and can be revoked at any time from within
        online banking. My relationship with my bank is governed by the bank's own terms; my use of
        Enable Banking is governed by Enable Banking's terms. Nothing on this page overrides either.
      </p>
      <p>
        How the data is handled once it reaches my computer is described in the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The application is provided as-is. It is a personal tool, written for my own use, with no
        guarantee of accuracy, availability, or fitness for any purpose. Figures it displays are for
        my own reference and are not financial advice, accounting records, or a substitute for
        statements issued by my bank. Where the application and the bank disagree, the bank is right.
      </p>

      <h2>No third-party access</h2>
      <p>
        Because there is no hosted service, there is nothing for anyone else to sign up to, log into,
        or misuse. If source code for the application is ever published, it will be published without
        credentials, without data, and without any working connection to a bank account.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may change if what the application does changes. The date at the top reflects the
        current version.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Belal Zaky — <a href="mailto:belal4606@gmail.com">belal4606@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-title {
      font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    }
  }

  .legal-dek {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 55ch;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
